pre_scan` so the error names the missing help artifact and points to `gen_cli_help.py`.","criteria":["error-handling","maintainability"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":"novelty-region","evidence":["src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py:89: `text = _help.subcommand_help(sub)`","src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py:93: `sys.stderr.write(f\"Error: unknown subcommand '{sub}'\\n\\n\")`","pre_scan reaches emit_subcommand_help only after `route is not None and _help_backed(route)` (src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py:154-156), so `sub` is a genuine registered route whose artifact is simply missing","Defended in practice: gen_cli_help.py `_check()` reports `missing artifacts` (scripts/gen_cli_help.py:204-212) in CI, so the mislabel only surfaces to a developer who added a route without regenerating help"],"finding":"When a visible, non-retired route exists in the registry but its committed help artifact is absent (e.g. a new intercept added before regenerating help), `pre_scan` routes a leading-help request through `emit_subcommand_help`, which calls `_help.subcommand_help(sub)`, gets `None`, and reports 'Error: unknown subcommand' to stderr with exit 1 — mislabeling a KNOWN route with a MISSING artifact as an unknown command rather than a clear 'missing/regenerate help' error.","id":"0","impact":0.0,"location":"src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py:83","norm_id":"n1aa9dc08412c60c2","novelty":1.0,"priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A developer adds a new visible intercept route to the registry, forgets to run `gen_cli_help.py`, and runs `rebar <newcmd> --help` before CI catches the drift"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_vi